From: Beaverfffan <1056715226@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] perf annotate: pass al_addr to hist_entry__tui_annotate

commit 1e0a0fffa4bb ("perf annotate: Add support to adjust offset of
source line") added a fourth al_addr argument to
hist_entry__tui_annotate(), but the call site in __cmd_annotate() was
only updated in the TUI-enabled branch of util/hist.h.  When perf is
built without TUI support the static inline stub in hist.h takes four
arguments, so the three-argument call in builtin-annotate.c fails to
compile:

  builtin-annotate.c:523:31: error: too few arguments to function
  'hist_entry__tui_annotate'

Pass 0 as al_addr, matching the behaviour when the symbol has no
synthesized address adjustment.

Signed-off-by: Beaverfffan <1056715226@qq.com>
---

--- a/tools/perf/builtin-annotate.c
+++ b/tools/perf/builtin-annotate.c
@@ -521,7 +521,7 @@
 			nd = rb_next(nd);
 		} else if (use_browser == 1) {
-			key = hist_entry__tui_annotate(he, evsel, NULL);
+			key = hist_entry__tui_annotate(he, evsel, NULL, 0);
 
 			switch (key) {
 			case -1:
